    <item>
      <title>BrainConnects 2026</title>
      <link>https://clinicalbrainlab.github.io/talk/2026_brainconnects/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 08:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://clinicalbrainlab.github.io/talk/2026_brainconnects/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;tags: [BrainConnects]
all_day: false
location: &amp;ldquo;Auditorium, Headquarters &amp;amp; Clinical Sciences Building (CSB), Nanyang Technological University&amp;rdquo;
address: &amp;quot;&amp;quot;
tags: [BrainConnects]
draft: false
url_code: &amp;quot;&amp;quot;
url_pdf: &amp;quot;&amp;quot;
url_slides: &amp;quot;&amp;quot;
url_video: &amp;quot;&amp;quot;
links:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;section style=&#34;max-width: 1120px; margin: 0 auto 2.5rem;&#34;&gt;
  &lt;img src=&#34;https://clinicalbrainlab.github.io/media/brainconnects/brainconnects-2026-logo.png&#34; alt=&#34;BrainConnects 2026 logo showing collaborating institutions connected by a brain network&#34; style=&#34;display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 0 auto 1.5rem;&#34;&gt;
  &lt;div style=&#34;width: calc(100% + 2.4rem); margin-left: -1.2rem; padding: 1.4rem; border: 1px solid rgba(15, 108, 109, 0.18); border-radius: 8px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #fbffff 0%, #eefafa 52%, #ffffff 100%); box-sizing: border-box;&#34;&gt;
    &lt;div style=&#34;max-width: 1120px; margin: 0 auto;&#34;&gt;
    &lt;p style=&#34;margin: 0 0 0.65rem; color: #0f6c6d; font-weight: 800; text-transform: uppercase;&#34;&gt;29 September - 2 October 2026&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;h2 style=&#34;margin-top: 0;&#34;&gt;Watch this page for BrainConnects 2026&lt;/h2&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; LKCMedicine HQ, Novena Campus, NTU, Singapore.&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;BrainConnects brings together researchers, clinicians, educators, engineers and technology partners working across cognitive neuroscience, neuroimaging, mental health, learning sciences and human development.&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;The 2026 meeting is hosted by the Science of Learning in Education Centre (SoLEC), National Institute of Education; the Centre for Lifelong Learning and Individualised Cognition (CLIC) NTU-Cambridge; the Centre of Research &amp;amp; Development in Learning (CRADLE), and the Cognitive Neuroimaging Centre (CoNiC) at NTU, with NIRx/Artinis as partners for the fNIRS workshop.&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;This year&#39;s theme, &lt;strong&gt;Shared Signals, Connected Learning&lt;/strong&gt;, reflects our interest in hyperscanning, portable imaging, fNIRS/EEG, and multimodal approaches to understanding connectedness, interpersonal synchrony, and shared attention in real-world learning environments. Learning rarely happens in isolation: it unfolds through exchanges between learners, teachers, peers, technologies, and environments. By studying shared neural, cognitive, physiological, behavioural, and social signals, BrainConnects 2026 aims to ask how people align attention, coordinate understanding, communicate meaning, and build knowledge together.&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;The timing is especially meaningful, as BrainConnects 2026 will also celebrate SoLEC&#39;s 5th Anniversary. This milestone broadens our research into how learners, educators, technologies, and environments become connected through shared neural, cognitive, physiological, and social signals, and how these insights can advance the science of learning.&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;div style=&#34;margin-top: 1.45rem; padding-top: 1.35rem; border-top: 1px solid rgba(15, 108, 109, 0.18);&#34;&gt;
      &lt;h3 style=&#34;margin: 0 0 0.9rem; color: #123d4a;&#34;&gt;Keynote Speakers&lt;/h3&gt;
